{"name":"Roadside","hex":"#ada493","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"roadside","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Located beside a road (or railway)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The area on either side of a road."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roadside"}],"entries":[{"title":"Road verge","blocks":[{"text":"A road verge is a strip of groundcover consisting of grass or garden plants, and sometimes also shrubs and trees, located between a roadway and a sidewalk. Verges are also known by other names such as easement, parkway, grass strip, nature strip, curb strip, berm, park strip, or tree lawn, the usage of which is often quite regional."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Massachusetts-devils_strip.JPG/330px-Massachusetts-devils_strip.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Road_verge","wikidata":"Q7339573"},{"title":"Shoulder (road)","blocks":[{"text":"A shoulder, hard shoulder or breakdown lane is an emergency stopping lane by the verge on the outer side of a road or motorway. Many wider freeways, or expressways elsewhere have shoulders on both sides of each directional carriageway—in the median, as well as at the outer edges of the road, for additional safety. Shoulders are not intended for use by through traffic, although there are exceptions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/SkHwy11ShoulderBumps.jpg/330px-SkHwy11ShoulderBumps.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoulder_(road)","wikidata":"Q1408712"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Roadside_Verge.jpg/500px-Roadside_Verge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Roadside_Verge.jpg/1280px-Roadside_Verge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Roadside_Verge.jpg/500px-Roadside_Verge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sign on a road verge in Northumberland, England, indicating that the verge is being managed by the local council to maintain populations of wild plants","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoadside_Verge.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/SEAR5.JPG/500px-SEAR5.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/SEAR5.JPG/1280px-SEAR5.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/SEAR5.JPG/500px-SEAR5.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pavements and planted strips in India ( Mumbai/Bombay)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASEAR5.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Treelawn2.JPG/500px-Treelawn2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Treelawn2.JPG/1280px-Treelawn2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Treelawn2.JPG/500px-Treelawn2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Planted rain garden in the \"tree lawn\" zone, Raleigh, North Carolina.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATreelawn2.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/20190830Cichorium_intybus1.jpg/120px-20190830Cichorium_intybus1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t